`verilator_config
// The UVM bench's own lint waiver (docs/decisions.md D-052). Verilator's WIDTH rules are meant for
// RTL: in class-based bench code they flag the standard idioms (`if (!x.randomize())`, the 64-bit
// uvm_reg_data_t arguments of the register API, $urandom_range results), and casting each one
// would bury the bench's logic. Every other Verilator warning stays an error for these files; the
// RTL stays -Wall clean (scripts/lint.sh).
lint_off -rule WIDTH -file "*testbench/uvm/*"
